| Right to erasure workflow | Employee consent withdrawal triggers the data erasure workflow for non-statutory data. Statutory data erasure is blocked at the platform layer. | Workflow — triggered on consent withdrawal | Enabled — DPDPA Phase 1 | Platform — enforced | M01 · DPDPA · P05 audit |
| PII redaction in audit log | Where non-statutory PII exists in the immutable audit log, it is overwritten with a redaction marker at erasure time. This is the only permitted mutation of the audit log — itself logged as a system erasure event. | System-initiated only — not admin action | System-controlled | Platform — not configurable | P05 Audit Log · DPDPA |
| Data principal request register | Right to erasure requests are tracked. Fulfillment for non-statutory data is documented. Legal basis recorded where erasure is not possible. | Register — HR Admin managed | Enabled — Phase 1 | HR Admin | DPDPA 2023 · P05 |

