# **Part G — Process Flows (Swimlane)**

High-level actor-level flows for the four highest-complexity admin setup scenarios. These are requirements-level flows — screen detail and field specifications belong in the functional specification.

Rows represent actors. Boxes are states or actions. Diamonds are decision points. Dashed lines are notifications.

## **G.1 New Tenant Provisioning Flow**

Actors: Platform Super Admin · Organisation Admin · HR Admin

Step 1 — Platform Super Admin selects industry segment (IT Services) and primary geography (India) at provisioning. Cascade load fires: leave policy defaults, performance framework, attendance model, payroll structure, workflow templates, statutory compliance scope, analytics defaults, holiday calendar pre-loaded.

Step 2 — Organisation Admin receives admin credentials. Configures company profile, logo, and registered address. Adds legal entities with entity-specific CIN, PAN, TAN, PF, and ESI codes.

Step 3 — Organisation Admin configures departments, designations, grades, and locations. Assigns HODs. Maps designations to grades and contribution levels.

Step 4 — HR Admin reviews and overrides entity-level configuration: leave policy assignments per grade, notice period per employment type, probation duration, separation reasons.

Step 5 — Org Admin configures authentication (SSO / password policy / MFA). Assigns roles to users. Creates UAGs for HRBP assignment.

Step 6 — Org Admin configures integrations (biometric devices, job boards, BGC vendor, calendar). Tests integrations. Reviews Integration Health dashboard.

Step 7 — Org Admin and HR Admin cross-reference Darwinbox Profile_View_settings export against RBAC §7. Documents discrepancies. Confirms Contractor role definition. Phase 1 gate criteria checked.

## **G.2 Individual Entitlement Grant Flow**

Actors: Requesting Manager / HRBP · Organisation Admin · System

Step 1 — Requesting party identifies access requirement beyond role default (e.g. HRBP temporarily covering a department not in their UAG). Communicates to Organisation Admin.

Step 2 — Org Admin validates request against PII protection ceiling (RBAC §1). If request would exceed PII ceiling, it is refused — no override path exists. If within ceiling, Org Admin proceeds.

Step 3 — Org Admin configures entitlement: type (department / field / section / module / contribution level), scope, and mandatory expiry date. Entitlement takes effect immediately.

Step 4 — System logs the grant: granting admin, user, entitlement type, effective date, expiry date. Logged in security audit log.

Step 5 — On expiry date, system automatically reverts user access to role default. No manual action required. HR Admin and Org Admin retain full coverage throughout — no gap in in-flight actions.

## **G.3 Darwinbox Profile View Settings Reconciliation Flow**

Actors: Implementation Lead · Organisation Admin · HR Admin

Step 1 — Implementation Lead exports Profile_View_settings.csv from Darwinbox and compares each field-role combination against RBAC §7 field-level access matrix.

Step 2 — For each discrepancy: (a) If Darwinbox showed a field to a role that PrimeSoft HRMS hides — this is an access reduction. Document and communicate to affected users before go-live. (b) If Darwinbox hid a field that PrimeSoft HRMS shows — this is a new exposure. Org Admin reviews and decides whether to suppress the field via individual entitlement configuration or accept the new visibility.

Step 3 — Org Admin signs off on the reconciliation. All discrepancies resolved or documented with business decision recorded. This is a Phase 1 go-live gate check.

## **G.4 Separation Reason**** ****&**** ****Deactivation Configuration Flow**

Actors: Org Admin · HR Admin · Implementation Lead

Step 1 — Implementation Lead exports Deactivation_Reasons-Export from Darwinbox. Reviews each entry for active vs archived status.

Step 2 — Active entries are mapped to PrimeSoft HRMS separation reason list. Voluntary/involuntary flag assigned per reason. Rehire eligibility default set per reason.

Step 3 — HR Admin provides the confirmed list of archived reasons to the Platform Super Admin. Platform Super Admin configures the P06 Migration Toolkit ETL to exclude archived reasons — per RBAC §4 and Product Vision v2.4 §3.8, no role other than Platform Super Admin has access to migration scripts or ETL configuration. HR Admin access to P06 is limited to entity-level data verification and field mapping review only.

Step 4 — Org Admin validates final separation reason list before go-live. HR Admin confirms rehire eligibility defaults align with HR policy.

# **Part H — Decision Log**

All confirmed decisions for Admin Settings. Changes to any locked decision require a recorded revision with date and decision owner.

| **#** | **Area** | **Decision** | **Note** | **Locked** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| AD01 | Financial year | Financial year starts in April for all Indian entities. Platform-enforced. Drives payroll year, leave cycle reset, and statutory compliance period. | Mandated by Indian statutory framework. | April 2026 |
| AD02 | Probation leave | Only Unpaid / LOP available during probation. All other leave types hidden. Platform-wide, non-configurable. Inherited from M04 D19. | Consistent with M04 locked decisions. | April 2026 |
| AD03 | Notice period leave | Only Sick Leave (if balance > 0) and Unpaid / LOP available during notice period. All other types hidden. Inherited from M04 D19. | Consistent with M04 locked decisions. | April 2026 |
| AD04 | National ID access | Office Admin can view and upload national identity documents (PAN, Aadhaar, Passport). This is a platform-level grant — fixed, not configurable by Org Admin upward or downward. Changes to field values require HR Admin approval workflow. | See RBAC §3.4 and §6. | April 2026 |
| AD05 | MFA enforcement | MFA enforced by default for HR Admin and Organisation Admin. These are the two roles with RBAC write access. Org Admin cannot disable MFA for these roles. MFA for other roles is Org Admin-configurable. | See Product Vision v2.4 §2.2 and RBAC §13. | April 2026 |
| AD06 | Contractor role | Contractor / Consultant role definition must be confirmed and implemented before Phase 1 go-live. The interim assumption (own attendance and documents, no payroll, not in directory) is not acceptable for production. Responsible owner: TBD. | Phase 1 gate criterion. See Product Vision v2.4 §1.7. | April 2026 |
| AD07 | PII ceiling | PII fields carry system-enforced protection ceilings. No Organisation Admin, Module Admin, or any other role can override these ceilings upward. This applies to all admin settings in this document — no admin action can expose government identifiers, financial data, biometric data, or health data beyond the defined permitted viewers. | See RBAC §1 and §6. Platform-enforced — not configurable. | April 2026 |
| AD08 | Audit log | Audit log entries are written by database-level trigger — not application code. No application bug, developer action, or API bypass can suppress an audit entry. Minimum retention: 7 years. Hard delete of statutory records blocked. | See Product Vision v2.4 §2.8. | April 2026 |
| AD09 | Profile view reconciliation | Darwinbox Profile_View_settings.csv must be cross-referenced against RBAC §7 before go-live. All discrepancies documented. Access reductions communicated to affected users. This is a Phase 1 go-live gate check. | Gate criterion — Org Admin sign-off required. | April 2026 |
| AD10 | Deactivation reasons migration | Archived deactivation reasons from Darwinbox must not be migrated as active. P06 Migration Toolkit ETL must be configured to exclude archived entries. Active reasons retain voluntary/involuntary classification and rehire eligibility defaults. | Migration gate — review required before Wave 1. | April 2026 |
| AD11 | UAG Head workflow approval authority | UAG Head workflow approval authority is a hard system ceiling — cannot be granted under any configuration. This is a platform-enforced ceiling, not a default setting. Org Admin has no configuration option to enable workflow approval authority for UAG Head users. HOD workflow approval authority remains configurable per workflow type per individual HOD user by Org Admin. | See RBAC §3.5 and Product Vision v2.4 §3.1. | April 2026 |
| AD12 | Analytics Admin scope | Analytics Admin is entity-scoped by default. Where tenant-wide report configuration is required, Org Admin may grant a tenant-scope individual entitlement to a designated Analytics Admin user. Both configurations are valid and audit-logged. | See RBAC §4 and Product Vision v2.4 §3.7 M16. | April 2026 |
| AD13 | HOD calendar | HOD does not see team leave on the calendar. HOD uses the dedicated team leave dashboard. HOD calendar visibility is fixed off — not configurable by Leave Admin or Org Admin. Inherited from M04 D28. | Consistent with M04 locked decisions. | April 2026 |
| AD14 | Bank disbursement | Bank disbursement files are never auto-transmitted. Payroll Admin initiates generation. Finance Admin approval required before release. This applies to all bank file types (NEFT and RTGS). | See Product Vision v2.4 §3.7 M06. | April 2026 |

# **Part I — Exception**** ****&**** ****Boundary Register**

Boundary conditions and exception scenarios for Admin Settings. Type: Confirmed = agreed as stated · Pending = requires business decision · Gate = Phase 1 go-live gate criterion.

| **#** | **Exception / boundary condition** | **System behaviour** | **Type** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| AE01 | Org Admin attempts to override PII protection ceiling | Blocked at the platform layer. No UI action available to expose government identifiers, financial, biometric, or health data beyond permitted viewers. Attempt logged in security audit log. | Confirmed |
| AE02 | Contractor / Consultant role not confirmed before go-live | Phase 1 go-live is blocked. The interim assumption is explicitly not acceptable for production. Responsible owner must confirm role definition. See AD06 and Product Vision v2.4 §1.7. | Gate |
| AE03 | Profile view discrepancy — Darwinbox field visible to role that is HIDDEN in PrimeSoft HRMS | Access reduction. Org Admin and Implementation Lead document the change. Affected users notified before go-live. No automatic restoration of Darwinbox visibility — PrimeSoft HRMS RBAC takes precedence. | Confirmed |
| AE04 | Org Admin attempts to grant an entitlement beyond PII ceiling | Blocked. Entitlement grant UI does not surface PII-ceiling fields for selection. If attempted through API, rejected with error. Attempt logged. | Confirmed |
| AE05 | Archived designation from Darwinbox assigned to an active employee | Designation marked inactive in PrimeSoft HRMS. Existing employee records retain the designation in read-only state. New assignments using this designation are blocked. HR Admin must update the employee record to an active designation. | Confirmed |
| AE06 | UAG Head granted workflow approval authority by Org Admin | Blocked. UAG Head workflow approval authority is a hard system ceiling — the configuration option does not appear for UAG Head users. HOD users have the configurable option. Org Admin attempting to grant to UAG Head receives an explicit system refusal. | Confirmed |
| AE07 | HR Admin changes PAN or Aadhaar field value directly | Blocked as a direct save. Changes to government identifier fields (PAN, Aadhaar, Passport Number) always route through an HR Admin approval workflow before the change is committed — per RBAC §7 (E · AR) and Product Vision v2.4 §2.5. Neither source specifies that a second HR Admin must approve — that is an unresolved workflow design question. The approval could be peer HR Admin, a self-confirmation step, or Organisation Admin sign-off. This must be resolved during functional design for M01 sensitive field change workflow. | Pending — approval chain within HR Admin tier to be confirmed during M01 functional design |
| AE08 | Biometric device offline during attendance capture | Device health heartbeat flag turns red in Integration Health dashboard. App check-in available as fallback where configured. Attendance records for the offline period are flagged for HR Admin review. Punch records sync when device reconnects — no data loss. | Confirmed |
| AE09 | Individual entitlement expires while an action is in progress | On expiry, user access reverts immediately to role default. Any in-flight approval actions initiated before expiry remain valid and can be completed by HR Admin or Org Admin within their normal scope. No gap in coverage. | Confirmed |
| AE10 | Two Org Admins simultaneously change the same RBAC rule | Last-write-wins. Both changes are audit-logged with timestamp and user. The system does not lock RBAC configuration for editing — Org Admins should coordinate out-of-band for simultaneous changes to critical rules. | Pending — concurrency handling to be confirmed |
| AE11 | Financial year start month change requested post-provisioning | Blocked — financial year start is a provisioning-time setting. Changing it post-provisioning would require data migration of leave balances, payroll records, and statutory compliance cycles. If required, must be raised as a formal change request to the Implementation Lead. | Confirmed |
| AE12 | Deactivation reason archived in Darwinbox but already used in existing separation records | The archived reason is excluded from new separation workflows. Existing separation records that reference the archived reason retain it in read-only historical state. HR Admin can view historical records with the archived reason — it appears as legacy data with an 'archived' indicator. | Confirmed |
| AE13 | Analytics Admin granted tenant-scope by Org Admin — what does this cover? | Tenant-scope Analytics Admin can create and publish custom report definitions visible across all entities within the tenant, and schedule tenant-wide report delivery. Data visibility within those reports is still governed by each individual user's own role entitlement — the Analytics Admin scope grant does not expand data access. Entity-scoped Analytics Admin operations remain restricted to their entity. | Confirmed |
| AE14 | Employee's location changed mid-month — which optional holiday quota applies? | Optional holiday quota applies based on the location active at the time of the optional holiday. If location changes mid-year, the new location's quota applies from the effective date of the change. HR Admin must review and adjust any pending optional holiday applications that pre-date the location change. | Pending — business rule to be confirmed |

# **Part J — Open Items ****&**** Next Steps**

## **J.1 Open decisions**

| **#** | **Area** | **Decision required** | **Recommended resolution** | **Owner** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| OD01 | Contractor / Consultant role | The Contractor role access definition (own attendance and documents, scoped to engagement period, no payroll visibility, not in directory) is an interim assumption. Final definition and ownership must be confirmed before Phase 1 go-live. | Confirm role definition and assign owner. Phase 1 gate criterion. | Org Admin · Implementation Lead |
| OD02 | Designation/Grade → Contribution level mapping | The tenant-level master mapping of designation and grade to RBAC contribution level (Intern · Associate · Individual Contributor · Lead · Senior Lead · Manager · Senior Manager · CEO) requires role assignment. No source document explicitly assigns this. | Inferred as Org Admin: contribution levels are an RBAC scoping dimension (RBAC §3.1) and RBAC configuration is Org Admin territory. HR Admin retains direct-edit on individual employee record per RBAC §7. Requires business sign-off. | Org Admin |

## **J.2 Migration gates**

| **#** | **Area** | **Action required before go-live** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| MG01 | Darwinbox Profile_View_settings reconciliation | Cross-reference Profile_View_settings.csv against RBAC §7 field-level access matrix. Document all discrepancies. Communicate access reductions to affected users. Org Admin sign-off required. See AD09 and G.3. |
| MG02 | Archived deactivation reasons | Configure P06 Migration Toolkit ETL to exclude archived separation reasons from Deactivation_Reasons-Export. Active reasons retain voluntary/involuntary classification and rehire eligibility defaults. See AD10 and G.4. |
| MG03 | Archived designations | Confirm active vs archived state for all designations in Designation_Names-Export before migration. Inactive designations must not migrate as Active. See A.4. |
| MG04 | Neev-Level-Export verification | Verify designation-to-contribution-level and grade-to-contribution-level mappings before migration. Pending OD02 resolution for ongoing ownership. See A.4 and A.5. |

